<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    What the installer is allowed to do under the hardened runtime, which notarisation requires.

    Both of these are about V8 rather than about the installer: a Javascript engine compiles as it
    runs, and the hardened runtime forbids writing memory and then executing it unless it is told
    that this is the point. Without them the executable is signed, notarised, and dies on startup.

    There is deliberately nothing else. The installer loads no library of its own, so library
    validation stays on; the native modules that would need it belong to the connector, which
    runs under the runtime in the payload and not under this signature.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
